  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Technical Assistance on Social Security policies provided</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">The ILO Cairo Office, has been supporting the Ministry of Social Solidarity (MoSS) on the social insurance and pension reform and the Government of Egypt since 2014 and it played an important role in drafting the new social insurance law of 2019. In the context of the COVID-19 pandemic, the related economic crisis exacerbated the social protection deficit of many informal economy workers.  ILO has been supporting the Egyptian government in the extension of social protection to informal workers and other vulnerable groups and in the implementation of the new social insurance law and the new health insurance law.

The objective of the of the ILO support is to support the government to undertakes a legislative reform in social protection and enhance the governance of social protection schemes and build the actuarial capacity of the national organization for social insurance to improve the financial management of the system. Another important outcome for the ILO support  is to support  the government in the extension of social protection to various uncovered groups such as informal workers, Egyptian working abroad, and refugees. 

The main beneficiaries of the ILO support are informal workers, refugees, and Egyptian working abroad. The main partners from the government side are NOSI, MoSS, UHIA, and MoF.</narrative>
  </description>
